        "They demand steady, criterion-by-criterion work spread across the autumn and winter terms, because most internal assessment deadlines, the Extended Essay's final draft and TOK's exhibition and essay all land between November and March of DP2 — well before the May exams, and often overlapping with the school's own mock-exam period. An IB DP tutor working with families in Spain plans backward from those specific school-set dates rather than from a generic syllabus calendar, because a school in Madrid and one in the Canary Islands rarely share the same internal deadlines.",
